  "_doc": "Binding table for sync-assets.py. Teritorija is ONE photograph and nothing else (2026-09-09). Filenames: <id>-<role>-<size>.webp; the role tag in a filename is historical. Two sizes are deliberately not round: dikis-mezs ships 1520 (exactly 2x its 760px crop) and K62 ships 2400 (exactly 2x its 1200px crop). When a web file is missing, the ORIGINAL is transcoded under that exact filename and listed in stand-ins.md. Paths are relative to photos/. min_crop values are binding floors. Since 2026-09-15: K25 out of Ara (8 tiles), K09 in first and K10 back in Otrais stavs (8 tiles, K09 served from its section file with its binding floor as tile attributes). no_balk was removed 2026-09-09: it is the autumn dawn version of the SAME view as the Teritorija lead E01, from the same vantage point, so with E01 in the section it read as a duplicate.",
